# Machine Learning Project - Predicting Exercise Movements

This project was completed as part of the Coursera Machine Learning course, focusing on predictive modeling using accelerometer data collected from wearable devices.

## Project Objective
The goal of this project is to predict the manner in which participants performed a barbell lift exercise. Using data collected from accelerometers on the belt, arm, forearm, and dumbbell, the target variable "classe" was modeled.

## Files Included
- `proyek_machine_learning.Rmd` — R Markdown file containing all code and explanation of the analysis process.
- `proyek_machine_learning.html` — Compiled HTML version of the R Markdown file for easy viewing.

## How to View
Open the `.html` file directly in your browser, or knit the `.Rmd` file again using RStudio.

